    "why": "Hear the crucial caution about “generational curses.” The speakers connect Exodus 34:7 with Exodus 20:5–6, where the pattern is explicitly tied to generations that continue in idolatry, and distinguish God’s just accountability of each generation from punishing innocent descendants for someone else’s sin. This clip also brings in Ezekiel 18 and John 9, showing that later biblical reflection resists simplistic inherited-guilt explanations while still acknowledging real intergenerational consequences.",
